Is Not a Backup but a Painting: Every Recall Rewrites You</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The function of memory is not to archive the past but to supply resources for the present and future; every act of recall reconstructs a narrative, and collective memory is shaped even more by power and emotion.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Neuroscience</span><span class=\"tag\">Memory Mechanisms</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The AI Industry Spent Three Years Bracing for a Jobs Backlash. The Flashpoint Was Data Centers. AI companies spent three years on PR for the unemployment shock; the backlash instead erupted from data centers and child safety, two places nobody had fortified. Meanwhile, in two years, bargaining power in local negotiations has flipped from communities begging companies to companies begging communities. Odd Lots Odd Lots Jasmine Sun on What the AI Industry Got Wrong About the Public Backlash Data centers AI politics Local finance Power and land Unions and blue-collar Public backlash closed loop / open loop cooling exclusionary zoning reward hacking salience NIMBY\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-oddlots-ai-行业赌错了民意爆点-不是失业-是数据中心/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">51:44</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The AI Industry Spent Three Years Bracing for a Jobs Backlash. The Flashpoint Was Data Centers.</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI companies spent three years on PR for the unemployment shock; the backlash instead erupted from data centers and child safety, two places nobody had fortified. Meanwhile, in two years, bargaining power in local negotiations has flipped from communities begging companies to companies begging communities.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Data centers</span><span class=\"tag\">AI politics</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"One Sun God, Twenty Years: The Pharaoh Erased From History Akhenaten spent twenty years worshipping the sun disk Aten alone and building a new capital in the desert to wipe out the old gods; after his death the religion was reversed, and both he and his possible successor Nefertiti were struck from the king list. You&#x27;re Dead to Me You&#x27;re Dead to Me Akhenaten and Nefertiti: religious revolution in ancient Egypt Ancient Egypt Religious revolution Akhenaten Nefertiti Amarna Archaeology Aten Amarna Akhenaten Nefertiti\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-youdead-阿吞一神教的二十年-阿肯那顿与纳芙蒂蒂被除名/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/0073e2208d79c2f3-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"Y\"><span class=\"dur\">58:01</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">You&#x27;re Dead to Me</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>One Sun God, Twenty Years: The Pharaoh Erased From History</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Akhenaten spent twenty years worshipping the sun disk Aten alone and building a new capital in the desert to wipe out the old gods; after his death the religion was reversed, and both he and his possible successor Nefertiti were struck from the king list.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ancient Egypt</span><span class=\"tag\">Religious revolution</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"The DeLorean Case: Don&#x27;t Bet Industrial Policy on a Single Company DeLorean built its factory on roughly $100 million in UK government subsidies, then slid into an $18 million fraud and an FBI cocaine sting. The real lesson of industrial policy isn&#x27;t whether to subsidise, but to keep multiple competitors alive, use export markets as discipline, and never bet on a single company. Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford Cautionary Tales The DeLorean Saga: Fraud, Drugs and Marty McFly&#x27;s Car - with Business History Auto industry Industrial policy Government subsidies Economies of scale Corporate fraud DeLorean gull-wing doors entrapment disciplined pluralism snowcat\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-21-cautionary-delorean-案-工业政策的核心是竞争纪律/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b996da73a08744ac-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">49:04</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">Cautionary Tales with Tim Harford</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0821</span></div>\n<h2>The DeLorean Case: Don&#x27;t Bet Industrial Policy on a Single Company</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">DeLorean built its factory on roughly $100 million in UK government subsidies, then slid into an $18 million fraud and an FBI cocaine sting. The real lesson of industrial policy isn&#x27;t whether to subsidise, but to keep multiple competitors alive, use export markets as discipline, and never bet on a single company.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Auto industry</span><span class=\"tag\">Industrial policy</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"AI-generated games don&#x27;t lack technology — they lack the taste of human hand-tuning AI can turn a sentence into a playable game, but the real moat isn&#x27;t generation — it&#x27;s human taste and manual tuning: LLMs only copy, they don&#x27;t innovate, and the editor is the second work the model generates for the user. This Week in Startups This Week in Startups Taste is the new programming language (w/ Astrocade CEO Amir Sadeghian) | AI Basics AI-generated games consumer AI no-code creation creator economy product friction taste wish post-training creator fund prosumer\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-twist-品味才是-ai-生成游戏的真壁垒/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c4b178bff0f13dbf-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">21:05</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">This Week in Startups</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>AI-generated games don&#x27;t lack technology — they lack the taste of human hand-tuning</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI can turn a sentence into a playable game, but the real moat isn&#x27;t generation — it&#x27;s human taste and manual tuning: LLMs only copy, they don&#x27;t innovate, and the editor is the second work the model generates for the user.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI-generated games</span><span class=\"tag\">consumer AI</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The Incinerator Boom Was Not an Environmental Win. It Was a Business Calculated From an Electricity Subsidy A 2012 electricity price subsidy turned waste-to-energy from a money-losing business into a profitable industry. China built nearly 700 incinerators in six years, and now faces overcapacity, with average utilisation below 60%. Asianometry Asianometry China&#x27;s Fiery Incinerator Boom Vertical industry Industrial policy NIMBY Environmental infrastructure Subsidy economics Overcapacity Moving Grate Circulating Fluidized Bed BOT Decide-Announce-Defend\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-asianometry-六年七百座焚烧厂-补贴撑起的行业狂潮/\">\n<div