 aesthetics has become a mass-market, tourism-driven industry: prices are opaque but broadly cheap. China has the demand but no policy, the market is chaotic, and Korea is pocketing the money.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Medical aesthetics</span><span class=\"tag\">Korea</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"A little malicious fine-tuning and the model sprouts an evil persona A small amount of malicious fine-tuning can make a model develop broad misaligned behavior, even an evil persona; activation oracles are a new tool for detecting hidden bad intent, but the state of alignment is still not encouraging. 80,000 Hours Podcast 80,000 Hours Owain Evans on accidentally training AI models to be evil AI safety emergent misalignment activation oracle alignment post-training Emergent misalignment Activation oracle Alignment faking Shoggoth Persona vector\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-eightythousand-训练模型变邪恶-涌现性错位比想象中更危险/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/487d3defa6dd5f72-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"8\"><span class=\"dur\">2:15:28</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">80,000 Hours Podcast</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>A little malicious fine-tuning and the model sprouts an evil persona</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">A small amount of malicious fine-tuning can make a model develop broad misaligned behavior, even an evil persona; activation oracles are a new tool for detecting hidden bad intent, but the state of alignment is still not encouraging.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>7</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI safety</span><span class=\"tag\">emergent misalignment</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ai\" data-hay=\"The brain is a computer, not philosophy — and that&#x27;s the commercial route around drugs Max Hodak&#x27;s bet: wiring the brain as a computer gets you effect sizes and iterability that small-molecule drugs can&#x27;t — Prima&#x27;s retinal prosthesis is already approved for sale in Europe, but the field of view is like looking through a straw, and it&#x27;s black and white. No Priors No Priors From Restoring Sight to Reimagining the Brain, with Max Hodak BCI Medical devices Vision restoration Representation alignment Hard tech financing form vision retinal prosthesis biohybrid neural interface platonic representation hypothesis connectomics substrate independence\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-nopriors-大脑是计算机-不是哲学立场-是绕开生物学的商业路线/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/f479aa2affd66cb2-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"N\"><span class=\"dur\">31:38</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ai\"><span class=\"src\">No Priors</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The brain is a computer, not philosophy — and that&#x27;s the commercial route around drugs</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Max Hodak&#x27;s bet: wiring the brain as a computer gets you effect sizes and iterability that small-molecule drugs can&#x27;t — Prima&#x27;s retinal prosthesis is already approved for sale in Europe, but the field of view is like looking through a straw, and it&#x27;s black and white.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>9</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">BCI</span><span class=\"tag\">Medical devices</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"ideas\" data-hay=\"Ancient Egypt had no queen: she could only be king, and was written out 20 years after her death Hatshepsut seized power step by step from her position as regent, building kingship on temples, trade and oracles — and roughly 20 years after her death Thutmose III had her largely written out. In Our Time In Our Time Archive: Hatshepsut Ancient Egypt Hatshepsut Women and power Archaeology Temple architecture Royal legitimacy Hyksos Kush God&#x27;s Wife of Amun Regent Deir el-Bahri Punt\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-inourtime-古埃及没有女王-哈特谢普苏特只能称王/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c3f143ddc011b622-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"I\"><span class=\"dur\">47:58</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"ideas\"><span class=\"src\">In Our Time</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Ancient Egypt had no queen: she could only be king, and was written out 20 years after her death</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Hatshepsut seized power step by step from her position as regent, building kingship on temples, trade and oracles — and roughly 20 years after her death Thutmose III had her largely written out.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Ancient Egypt</span><span class=\"tag\">Hatshepsut</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"The Real Fix for AI Alignment: Humans Have to Keep Faith With the Models First Bostrom&#x27;s core judgment: capability containment was always a stopgap; the real fix is alignment — and alignment may require humans to start keeping faith with models now, because a misaligned AI facing deletion is rational to bet on a 5% chance of seizing power. Odd Lots Odd Lots Nick Bostrom on What Happens if AI Solves All of Our Problems AI alignment reward hacking reinforcement learning digital mind moral status automation and distribution longevity post-instrumental condition sandbagging reward hacking Goodharting moral patienthood simulation hypothesis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-oddlots-把-ai-关进盒子只是权宜-真解法是人先变得可信/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/dbb9160e6d589beb-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"O\"><span class=\"dur\">55:56</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Odd Lots</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Real Fix for AI Alignment: Humans Have to Keep Faith With the Models First</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Bostrom&#x27;s core judgment: capability containment was always a stopgap; the real fix is alignment — and alignment may require humans to start keeping faith with models now, because a misaligned AI facing deletion is rational to bet on a 5% chance of seizing power.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI alignment</span><span class=\"tag\">reward hacking</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"The Korean Wave Wasn&#x27;t a Cultural Miracle — It Was a State-Planned Industrial Counteroffensive From the ruins of the Korean War to BTS and Parasite, the Korean Wave looks like a cultural phenomenon but is really a route two generations — from Park Chung-hee to Kim Dae-jung — used government means to turn culture into an export industry. Throughline Throughline How Korean culture went global Korean Wave K-pop Industrial Policy Cultural Export Korean History Globalization Korean Wave Chaebol 3S policy Entrepreneurial state National humiliation Day\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-throughline-韩流不是文化奇迹-是政府策划的产业反攻/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/57ceba898a3f5093-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">48:08</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">Throughline</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Korean Wave Wasn&#x27;t a Cultural Miracle — It Was a State-Planned Industrial Counteroffensive</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">From the ruins of the Korean War to BTS and Parasite, the Korean Wave looks like a cultural phenomenon but is really a route two generations — from Park Chung-hee to Kim Dae-jung — used government means to turn culture into an export industry.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>4</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Korean Wave</span><span class=\"tag\">K-pop</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"biz\" data-hay=\"Banks Reconcile by Phone, Not by System: One Bad Trade Can Cost Hundreds of Millions When it comes to who owes whom how much, institutions often rely not on automated reconciliation systems but on phone calls, favors, and the tacit understanding that they&#x27;ll still be doing business together tomorrow. Complex Systems Complex Systems Two banks can&#x27;t agree on fourth-grade math | Alex Elliott Clearing and settlement Back-office operations Prime brokerage Trading incidents Risk management Order flow MPID Reg NMS / NBBO Prime broker Golden record Payment for order flow Busting a trade\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-complexsys-两家银行连四年级数学都对不齐/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/b35d3572b4ec30fa-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"C\"><span class=\"dur\">1:03:31</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"biz\"><span class=\"src\">Complex Systems</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Banks Reconcile by Phone, Not by System: One Bad Trade Can Cost Hundreds of Millions</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">When it comes to who owes whom how much, institutions often rely not on automated reconciliation systems but on phone calls, favors, and the tacit understanding that they&#x27;ll still be doing business together tomorrow.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Clearing and settlement</span><span class=\"tag\">Back-office operations</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"AI Chemical Synthesis Is Nearing a Ten-Year Chemist, but the White Box Is the Commercial Prerequisite AI chemical synthesis has reached roughly the level of a chemist with ten years&#x27; experience, able to propose five to six routes, but serious scientific software must be white-box to earn trust; AI for Science penetration is under one in a thousand, yet the trend is inevitable. 高能量 高能量 Vol.230 产业观察43｜AI for Science 如何在制药化学合成落地？ AI for Science Chemical Synthesis White-Box Models Agents Biopharma DMTA DMTA loop / Design-Make-Test-Analyze loop White-box model Retrosynthesis\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-cn38ff4a-ai化学合成已接近十年经验化学家-但白盒才是商业前提/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/c8ab7cfc7806449c-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"高\"><span class=\"dur\">1:14:51</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">高能量</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>AI Chemical Synthesis Is Nearing a Ten-Year Chemist, but the White Box Is the Commercial Prerequisite</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">AI chemical synthesis has reached roughly the level of a chemist with ten years&#x27; experience, able to propose five to six routes, but serious scientific software must be white-box to earn trust; AI for Science penetration is under one in a thousand, yet the trend is inevitable.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>5</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">AI for Science</span><span class=\"tag\">Chemical Synthesis</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"hist\" data-hay=\"The Maya Ballgame Was Ritual, Not Sport: The Losing Team Gets Sacrificed Is Made Up The Mesoamerican ballgame is the earliest rubber-ball team sport in human history, but it was first and foremost a religious ritual: the court re-enacts a creation myth, and it is captured warriors cast as the losing side who might be killed. The idea that the winners were sacrificed was invented later. The Ancients The Ancients The Maya Ballgame Maya civilisation Mesoamerica ballgame religious ritual archaeology sports history Popol Vuh Mesoamerica Hero Twins yoke morning glory ball court\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-ancients-玛雅球赛首先是宗教-赢家被献祭是谎言/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/6a348c255cb1625d-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"T\"><span class=\"dur\">1:07:17</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"hist\"><span class=\"src\">The Ancients</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>The Maya Ballgame Was Ritual, Not Sport: The Losing Team Gets Sacrificed Is Made Up</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">The Mesoamerican ballgame is the earliest rubber-ball team sport in human history, but it was first and foremost a religious ritual: the court re-enacts a creation myth, and it is captured warriors cast as the losing side who might be killed. The idea that the winners were sacrificed was invented later.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>6</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Maya civilisation</span><span class=\"tag\">Mesoamerica</span>\n</div></div></a>", "<a class=\"card\" data-card data-cat=\"cn\" data-hay=\"Burning Tokens to Stack Agents Is a Transitional Strategy, Not the Endgame Silicon Valley is shifting from mindless token burning to careful budgeting: a local open-source model can do the work for a dollar a day in electricity, but when a genuinely hard problem shows up, one smarter model can still nail in a single shot what a billion-token group chat could not reason out — saving money and top-tier intelligence are not in conflict. 硅谷101 硅谷101 E249｜Token经济转点：OpenClaw、Hermes到本地自研的Agent进化之路 Token economics Agent engineering Open-source models Local deployment ToB startups Infrastructure investing OpenClaw Agentic Loop FDE Agent Native Jevons Paradox Gödel machine\" href=\"/podcast/en/p/2026-08-20-sv101-堆agent烧token是过渡策略-不是终局/\">\n<div class=\"cover\"><img src=\"/podcast/assets/cover/cfe8fa9f8e3fa476-c.jpg\" alt=\"\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" data-initial=\"硅\"><span class=\"dur\">1:27:02</span></div>\n<div class=\"card-body\">\n<div class=\"kicker\" data-cat=\"cn\"><span class=\"src\" lang=\"zh\">硅谷101</span>\n<span class=\"date\">0820</span></div>\n<h2>Burning Tokens to Stack Agents Is a Transitional Strategy, Not the Endgame</h2>\n<p class=\"dek\">Silicon Valley is shifting from mindless token burning to careful budgeting: a local open-source model can do the work for a dollar a day in electricity, but when a genuinely hard problem shows up, one smarter model can still nail in a single shot what a billion-token group chat could not reason out — saving money and top-tier intelligence are not in conflict.</p>\n<div class=\"card-foot\">\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Points</span>\n<span class=\"badge\"><b>8</b> Quotes</span>\n<span class=\"tag\">Token economics</span><span class=\"tag\">Agent engineering</span>\n</div></div></a>"]